```
When the state is 2 (Initialized), we capture `pts: &'static PointsTo<Option<T>>` into `readonly_points_to`. This satisfies the `is_Some()` precondition for `tracked_borrow()` and the `id()`/`is_init()` preconditions for `cell.borrow()`.

### 2. Compare-exchange ghost block (transitioning 0→1)
```rust
match g {
    GhostState::Uninitialized(p) => {
        points_to = Some(p);        // ← extract PointsTo for initialization
        g = GhostState::Initializing;
    }
    GhostState::Initializing => { g = GhostState::Initializing; }
    GhostState::Initialized(pts) => { g = GhostState::Initialized(pts); }
}
```
When the CAS succeeds (value was 0 = Uninitialized), we extract the `PointsTo` into outer `points_to` and transition the ghost state to `Initializing`. This satisfies the `is_Some()` precondition for `tracked_unwrap()`.

### 3. Store ghost block (transitioning to state 2)
```rust
g = GhostState::Initialized(static_points_to);
```
After storing value 2, we set the ghost state to `Initialized` with the now-static PointsTo reference, satisfying the atomic invariant.
